      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-07-24_WidnesExaminer_art0258" n="art0258">
        <head>NOTES BY "THE JACK."</head>
        <p>NOTES BY "THE JACK."</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON WORKS AMATEUR</p>
        <p>ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>Keen Games In Third Round For " Finlayson " Cup.</p>
        <p>Four interesting ties in the third round of the " Finlayson" Cup Competition were played off on the Horse and Jockey green on Saturday afternoon, in the presence of a good number of bowling enthusiasts. The first of the quartette of games were between Pearson and Knowles' Engineers and Fletcher, Russell's men. Eight of the twelve ends were decided in favour of the F. and R. players, who subsequently ran out victorious by an aggregate majority of 29 points. The second game was between the Whitecross Netting Department and Cros- field's V. 8., and it produced some excellent and even bowling, and though :no. fewer than eight out of the dozen ends fell to the Whitecross men they were in the lump only 4 points better than their opponents. The Cheshire Lines No 2 team were pitted against the Bewsey Wire Ropery's representatives, and again the struggle was a good one, though the margin by which the railwaymen won was the second big, gest of the afternoon, viz., 29. The Firth Mat- tress Co.'s men and the Assurance Agents first combination were wonderfully evenly matched, the -agents running out ninners by a bare point. Below will be found the detailed scores:—</p>
