        <p>Every person to whom the Act applies-must fill up and sign a separate registration form, and all who have duly filled up and signed a form will receive a certificate of registration, which must be signed and preserved. Above we. reproduce a copy of the form that will be delivered by the enumerators. Any person who is willing to render voluntary service in connection with the work of regis- tration is requested to communicate with the Town Clerk forthwith, stating present occupa- tion and the hours when they will be available for delivering and collecting the forms, •or whether they prefer clerical work in the office. Further details concerning the registration will be found in our advertisement columns. The Rural District Council of Runcorn are also scliciting offers of voluntary assistance in the matter of the compilation of the register in their area. Offers of assistance should be addressed to -Mr. W. E. Hough, the acting- clerk to the Rural District Council, 71, High- street, Runcorn, not late): WA .IS.t Riia on tho morning of July 20t1t.</p>
