        <p>The forms themselves will constitute the register and will be arranged in index form, and it is therefore desirable that they should he kept flat and not folded in any way, other- wise the work of' the enumerators will be con- siderably interfered with. Nothing can be gained by residents folding the papers and placing them in envelopes, for the enumerators will have instructions to read the papers at each house at which they call in order to assure themselves that th 9 iagrraidi.9ll GOpvlird i 5 =nal</p>
