        <p>is-t-O-UNTY BOROUGH OF W ARMIN-4:1'61r 1,-) NATIONAL REGISTRATION ACT, 1915. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the Registration required by the above Act of all persons' (male and female) between the ages of 15 and 65 (subject to certain exceptions) will be made on Sunday, the 15th day of August, 1915. Forms will be delivered on one or more of the six days immediately preceding the _ls..th August, and the Forms must be filled up read for collection by Monday, August 16th. Every person to whom the Act applies must fill up and sign a separate Registration Form. Any person who may not have received a Form on or before Monday, the 16th August, or who may have lost or dectroyed the Perm or may have been otherwise. Prevented from filling up the Form within the prescribed time, can pro- cure one at any of the following places; but Forms so obtained must be filled up, signed and delivered at any of such places not later than noon on Wednesday, the 18th August:— T,he Gymnasium, Palmyra-square. The Bolton Council Schocl (boys' entrance). , The Emmanuel Church Institute at corner of ' Knutsford-road and School-street. Evelyn-street Council School (girls' entrance) St. Barnabas' School, Bostock-street. Silver-street School. The Ileamont Council School ( infants' entrance). The National School, Church-street. (Persons are requested to attend between the hours of 12 and 2 and 5 and 8 p.m) Every person who has duly filled up and signed his Registration Form will receive a Certificate of Registration, which must be signed and preserved by him. Every assistance will be rendered by the staff of the Local Registration Authority and ' by the duly appointed Enumerators, but it would be convenient if applications for assist- ance or advice were made at the Central Office at the Gymnasium, Palmyra-square. The Central Office will be open from 9 a.m. till 8 p.m. Any lady or gentleman who is willing to render Voluntary Service is requested to com- municate with the Town Clerk forthwith, and to state present occupation, hours willing to devote, whether willing to deliver and collect Registration Forms, or prefers clerical work in. the office in filling up Forms, indexing and the preparation of the Register. J. LYON wuirr-LE. • Town Clerk.</p>
