        <p>WARRINGTON RURAL DISTRICT COUN- CIL—THE WARRINGTON RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL are PREPARED TO RECEIVE TENDERS from persons willinv 4-o CON'rRA CT Fi'lt THE REMOVAL i CONTENTS WI THE PAILS AND ASHTUBS upon property within the township of Great Sankey. The Contractor must remove the ashes and the contents of the pails once in every week, the same to be properly cleansed and disinfected. The contents of the pails to be removed in a suitable covered cart to be provided by the Con- tractor at his own cost. Also for the Emptying and Cleansing of all Privies and Ashpits in the same township at least once in every three months, and oftener if so required. The work of emptying the pails, privies and ashpits to be com- pleted before nine o'clock in the morning of each day, and all places where nightsoil has been deposited to be treated with disinfectants to be supplied by the Council to the Contractor. The termination of the Contract will require three months' notice in writing by either side. Tenders must be, delivered not later than twelve o'clock on Tuesday, the 3rd August, endorsed "Tender for nightsoil, Any further particulars may be obtained by applying to Mr. F. W. Kerfoot, Inspector. Bewsey Chambers, Warrington. By Order, J. C. SUTTON, Clerk to the Council. Bewsey Chambers, Warrington, July 17th, 1915.</p>
