        <p>FRANK GANNON. Prisoner in Germany.</p>
        <p>captured that I got hit and then the parapet was blown in on me and I was buried and had to crawl out the best way I could. This happened early in the morning and I lay in the trench until midnight without a bite to eat. The enemy were bombarding us con- stantly. When it was safe to get away I crawled about two miles to a dressing station. It took me all night to do it." The brother to whom the letter Is addressed, Private Thomas Gallon, is at present serving</p>
