        <p>VICTORIOUS PADGATE BMA LEItS. A Penketh Team Beaten By Big Margin. A team of Padgate bowlers on Saturday after- noon, met the representatives of the Heath-road (Penketh) Bowling Club, and defeated them both in the singles and the doubles, having an aggregate advantage of 68 points. The total sores were: Padgate, singles 142, doubles 101; Heath-road, 90 and 85. The individual scores are set out below ; Singles. W. Buckley 11, R. Graham 7. J. Appleton 11, A. SkelhoLae 9. E. Lunt 11, J. Jackson 5. R. W. Cook 11, W. Leah 7. J. Seed 11, H. Glover 4. It. Tunstall 11, Phil. Johnson 2. W. G. Profitt 5, W. Smith 11. F. Wright 11, A. Platt 8. E. England 11, E. ,Glover 6. A. Lamb 11, 11. Dobbins 0. I, Angus 5, A. James 11. F. J. nopkins 11, C. Monks 8. J. A. Proffitt 11, J. Ray 6. W. Mitchell 11, A. Skelhorn 6. Doubles. Buckley and Appleton 15, Graham and Sk-el- home 14. Lunt-And Cook 15, Jackson and. Leah 13. Seed and Tunstall 15, Glover and Johnson 6. Profitt and Wright 15, Smith and Platt 14. England and Lamb 15, Glover and Dobbins 11 Angus and Hopkins 11, James and Monks 15. Profitt and Mitchell 15, Ray and Skelhorn 12.</p>
